  "description": "<p>St Lawrence College is a College of Applied Arts and Technology with three campuses in Eastern Ontario: Brockville, Cornwall, and Kingston. The College has a long history of academic excellence, as it was first established in 1856.</p><p>Around 212 international students are enrolled in courses at the College yearly, in popular courses such as Business Administration and Computer Programming. Situated rurally, the institution prioritises high-quality teaching with good value for money in tuition.</p><h2>What is the St Lawrence College acceptance rate for International Students?</h2><p>The St Lawrence College acceptance rate is 57%.</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>Campus life is rich and varied for students at St Lawrence College. Students are engaged in over 100 student clubs and organisations, with politically active and sporty students finding ways to socialise together. The food options on campus cater to a range of tastes, and technological advancement enables students to enjoy leisurely activities in addition to academic goals. The student support services available also empower students to achieve their full potential.</p><p>Ontario is a part of Canada with lots of students and beaches. Student satisfaction tends to be high as the nightlife is built for young people to enjoy, and the scenery inspires academic prowess and mental well-being. The natural attractions draw many tourists in and allow students to enjoy a range of eateries, shops, and other activities.</p>",
