      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>St. Lawrence College has four residences with different amenities and room configurations. The residences are located on or near campus, making them convenient for students. Students can apply for a place by completing the residence application form and paying a deposit. Homestay programs are popular for students as they can stay with a local Canadian family to improve their English and settle into local life.</p><p>Students often live off-campus in privately-owned apartments, houses, or shared accommodations. St. Lawrence College provides various resources to help students find off-campus housing, including an online housing board and a housing registry.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sports",
      "value": "<p> St. Lawrence College has a state-of-the-art athletic and fitness centre with a gymnasium, weight room, indoor track, and group fitness classes. The college has outdoor facilities, including soccer fields, tennis courts, and a running track. St. Lawrence College has an on-campus health clinic staffed by licensed healthcare professionals. The clinic provides various services, including medical consultations, vaccinations, and specialist referrals.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Library",
      "value": "<p>St Lawrence College has a vast library of books and other literary resources. Computer workstations, study rooms, and scanning facilities are easily found throughout the library and several communal study spaces.",
